Subject: Replace PTR_SIZE_INT data/function pointer bitmasking in crypto/bn/bn_nist.c
Policy-Class: P4-Audit
Rationale: OpenSSL 1.1.1's BN_nist_mod_{192,224,256,384,521} cast BN_ULONG* and bn_addsub_f function pointers to PTR_SIZE_INT, bitmask them, and cast back to pointers, which strips Fil-C capability provenance and traps at runtime. Use constant-time word-level selection (nist_ct_select_bn) and direct function-pointer selection instead, matching OpenSSL 3.x's provenance-safe approach.
Upstream-Status: Backport (fixed upstream in OpenSSL 3.x)
Fil-C-Origin-Commits: original

diff --git a/crypto/bn/bn_nist.c b/crypto/bn/bn_nist.c
--- a/crypto/bn/bn_nist.c
+++ b/crypto/bn/bn_nist.c
@@ -279,6 +279,16 @@
 
     for (i = 0; i < top; i++)
         dst[i] = src[i];
+}
+
+static void nist_ct_select_bn(BN_ULONG *dst, const BN_ULONG *if_zero,
+                              const BN_ULONG *if_nonzero, int top,
+                              BN_ULONG mask)
+{
+    int i;
+
+    for (i = 0; i < top; i++)
+        dst[i] = (if_nonzero[i] & mask) | (if_zero[i] & ~mask);
 }
 
